# .github/CODEOWNERS
# Remediation: R-13
#
# Enforces review requirements per directory and file type.
# All rules are additive — a file matching multiple patterns requires
# approval from ALL matching teams.
#
# Format: pattern   @team-or-user
# Patterns are evaluated in order; last match wins for the default reviewer,
# but GitHub shows ALL matching owners as required reviewers.
#
# IMPORTANT: Team slugs must match your GitHub organization's team names.
# Update @your-org/... references to match your actual org and team slugs.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Global fallback — platform lead reviews anything unmatched ────────────────────
*                                       @your-org/ml-platform-lead

# ── Runbooks and decision trees (SRE review required) ───────────────────────────
runbooks/                               @your-org/ml-platform-sre
diagrams/                               @your-org/ml-platform-sre
severity_matrix.md                      @your-org/ml-platform-sre
incident_response_template.md           @your-org/ml-platform-sre

# ── Governance (governance board approval required) ────────────────────────────
governance.md                           @your-org/ml-governance-board
docs/operational_principles.md          @your-org/ml-governance-board
SECURITY.md                             @your-org/ml-governance-board @your-org/ml-security-team

# ── CI/CD and infrastructure (security + platform lead) ─────────────────────────
ci_cd/                                  @your-org/ml-security-team @your-org/ml-platform-lead
.github/                                @your-org/ml-security-team @your-org/ml-platform-lead
infrastructure/                         @your-org/ml-security-team @your-org/ml-platform-lead
Dockerfile.dev                          @your-org/ml-security-team
.dockerignore                           @your-org/ml-security-team
requirements.txt                        @your-org/ml-security-team @your-org/ml-platform-engineering
pyproject.toml                          @your-org/ml-platform-engineering

# ── Application source (platform engineering review) ───────────────────────────
api/                                    @your-org/ml-platform-engineering
src/                                    @your-org/ml-platform-engineering
pipelines/                              @your-org/ml-platform-engineering
orchestration/                          @your-org/ml-platform-engineering

# ── Monitoring and observability (SRE + ML engineers) ──────────────────────────
monitoring/                             @your-org/ml-platform-sre @your-org/ml-engineers
observability/                          @your-org/ml-platform-sre
dashboards/                             @your-org/ml-platform-sre

# ── dbt models (data engineering review) ───────────────────────────────────────
dbt/                                    @your-org/ml-data-engineering
configs/                                @your-org/ml-data-engineering @your-org/ml-platform-engineering

# ── ML models (ML engineering review) ──────────────────────────────────────────
ml_models/                              @your-org/ml-engineers
